WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.110
Batman V Superman's theatrical release was
2 and a half hours long, but we'll be getting

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:09.420
an extended R-rated cut with the Blu-ray and
DVD release which Zack Snyder has dubbed the

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.420
Ultimate Cut.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.650
So, what didn't make it into the final movie
and what other unused concepts may we see

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.709
in future movies?

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:19.860
Just before kicking off, I've got a fantastic
giveaway from our friends at Titan Books for

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.530
the official tech manual for Batman V Superman:
Dawn of Justice.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.970
Inside this fab hardback book are tons of
amazing concept art, an exclusive look at

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.160
Batman's arsenal, vehicles, Batsuits, and
Batcave, as well as Superman's Kryptonian

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.710
suit and Wonder Woman's iconic weaponry.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.420
For a chance to win, subscribe and leave a
comment about the deleted scenes or what you'd

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.359
like to see in the extended cut of Batman
V Superman.

00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:46.030
For more details and ways to enter, check
out the Gleam link in the video description

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.030
below!

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.469
OK, quick spoiler warning, obviously if you
haven't seen Batman V Superman yet, I'll be

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:54.399
discussing a ton of spoilers so come back
as soon as you've had a chance to see the

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:55.399
movie.

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:59.239
First up, there was a much longer opening
sequence filmed with Lois Lane in the African

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:02.410
village Nairomi that will be included in the
extended cut.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:06.800
In the longer scene, the unnamed undercover
CIA op who was with Lois, reveals himself

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.110
as Daily Planet photographer Jimmy Olsen and
tells Lois he's been assigned to her for the

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.110
mission.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.220
Director Zack Snyder had originally hoped
to cast Jesse Eisenberg as Jimmy Olsen which

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.370
he felt would create a real WTF moment when
the character was killed right at the beginning

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.530
of the movie, especially because Eisenberg
is a well-known actor.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.780
Snyder has defended his decision to kill off
the beloved DC character saying that there

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:33.180
wasn't "room for Jimmy Olsen" in the current
DC movie universe that Warner Bros is building.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.470
Jena Malone filmed some scenes that we can
definitely look forward to in the Ultimate

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:37.470
Cut.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:42.030
Her role is still unconfirmed, although Zack
Snyder has said she isn't Robin or Batgirl.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.690
Based on what we know so far, Malone is likely
playing Oracle, a computer hacker in the comics

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.570
who provides tech support to a range of superheroes.

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:53.660
In The Killing Joke graphic novel, the Joker
shot Barbara Gordon, paralysing her, which

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.270
led her to become Oracle.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:59.880
Another hint towards this theory is that in
DC's TV universe, when Green Arrow was wondering

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.870
what codename to give Felicity Smoak, he said
that Oracle was already taken.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:08.330
Although the TV and film universes are separate,
it could be a cheeky little hint that we'll

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.129
be seeing Oracle on the big screen.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:15.920
A scene was filmed in 2013 at East LA College
for a football game at Gotham City University

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.480
stadium between the home team and Metropolis
State University.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.980
It seems that this scene could be an introduction
to Vic Stone, aka Cyborg, who is a football

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.390
player in the comics.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:29.150
It's possible that some kind of tragedy or
terrible injury happened to Vic at the football

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.469
game which is why we see him with missing
arms and legs later just before he's turned

00:02:33.469 --> 00:02:36.140
into Cyborg by the motherbox at Star Labs.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:39.709
"Ahman Green, the [former] running back from
the Green Bay Packers" is credited in the

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:44.129
film as Thug #2 and he's confirmed to be in
the extended cut and may have something to

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:45.129
do with this scene.

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:49.519
The supervillain Metallo was originally going
to be the key villain in the Man of Steel

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:50.519
sequel.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:54.590
In the comics, Metallo is a cyborg who uses
kryptonite as his power source and was created

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:59.110
by the scientist Emmet Vale who, like Lex
Luthor in Batman V Superman, was concerned

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.380
about Superman's power.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:05.189
But when they decided to make Batman V Superman
rather, than a standalone Superman sequel,

00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:08.269
the idea of having Metallo as the villain
was put on ice.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:13.060
However, Metallo's creator Emmet Vale, played
by actor Ralph Lister, did appear in the movie

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.480
working at the Lexcorp lab, leaving the path
open for the villain to appear in a future

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.480
film.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.140
Zack Snyder has said that Batman villains
the Joker and Riddler were almost put in Batman

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.140
V Superman.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.040
However, Snyder and screenwriter Chris Terrio
later felt their addition would be a distraction

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.459
from the main protagonists Batman and Superman.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:32.709
But the supervillains' presence is still felt
in a number of easter eggs that made their

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:36.790
way into the movie such as the Riddler and
Joker graffiti that litters the run-down building

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:41.079
where Batman and Superman fight and the Joker
graffiti all over the defaced Robin suit.

00:03:41.079 --> 00:03:45.489
On the subject of dead Robin, his weapon,
which you see together with his suit in the

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:48.430
Batcave, was originally built as a fully intact
piece.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:53.079
Later, Snyder decided that the weapon needed
to be shown broken as a further hint at what

00:03:53.079 --> 00:03:55.279
happened to Robin at the hands of the Joker.

00:03:55.279 --> 00:03:59.230
By the way, the Batwing was also designed
with a second seat which is where Robin would

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:03.180
have sat before he was killed ten years before
the events of Batman V Superman.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.769
Since that happened, Bruce Wayne has modified
the empty space to use it as convenient storage

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:09.739
for an extra set of guns.

00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:13.819
The Batwing was designed to have folding wings
so that when it's in the Batcave and covered

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.680
with a tarp it looks and hangs just like a
bat.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.730
The Batwing did of course appear in the theatrical
release, but we didn't get to see the folding

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:21.730
wings.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:25.500
Also, production designer Patrick Tatopoulos
said it was crucial that Batman had the ability

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.169
to take off and land anywhere, even an alley.

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:32.349
So, the designers also made sure the Batwing
had the ability to take off vertically and

00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:37.090
they even ran a CG test to prove the Batwing
could do just that, even though this didn't

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.759
happen in the final film.

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:43.180
Henry Cavill was spotted filming scenes outside
the Gotham City jail and producer Deborah

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.750
Snyder has confirmed that scenes where Clark
Kent visits Gotham to look into Batman's activities

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.430
more closely will appear in the extended cut.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.810
Bodybuilder CT Fletcher has confirmed he was
on set for a prison scene, so it looks like

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:58.280
we'll get to see more details about Clark
Kent's investigation into some of the Bat

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.710
vigilante's victims.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:04.120
Dan Amboyer, who starred in the TV comedy
Younger, has said he was on the set of Batman

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:08.120
V Superman "right at the beginning of shooting"
and that he played a character called Lieutenant

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.120
Christie.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.580
On IMDB he's credited as "Drone Pilot" and
it's been rumoured he could end up as one

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.270
of the Green Lanterns.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:18.030
It remains to be seen whether what he filmed
makes it into the extended cut and whether

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:21.580
we'll get a tease for Green Lantern in Batman
V Superman or if we'll have to wait for the

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.550
first Justice League movie.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.550
Just after the opening weekend for Batman
V Superman, Warner Bros released an intriguing

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.570
deleted scene titled "Communion".

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:32.900
In it we see a SWAT team descend into the
Kryptonian scout ship, The Fortress of Solitude,

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.080
where they find Lex Luthor communing with
a demonic-looking creature.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.360
The creature feels like it might hail from
Darkseid's planet Apokolips, and its look

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.879
best matches Darkseid's father Yuga Khan.

00:05:42.879 --> 00:05:48.009
Other alternatives could be Steppenwolf, one
of Darkseid's generals or even possibly the

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:50.980
DCEU's version of Darkseid himself.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:55.220
Darkseid was already teased in the main theatrical
release via the Omega symbol that Bruce Wayne

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:56.930
sees in his Knightmare.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:01.900
In this deleted scene, there are also 3 motherboxes
and an orb floating above the demonic creature

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.509
and they all dissolve away as the soldiers
reach Lex.

00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:09.319
It looks like Lex is learning about Darkseid
and his forces via holographic images.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:13.410
The moment calls back to when Clark Kent returned
to the scout ship in Man of Steel and learned

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.889
about Krypton and the universe from his father
Jor-El.

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:20.350
The deleted scene helps to tie up the easter
eggs from the theatrical release, like Lex

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.599
Luthor's mention of gods falling from the
sky when talking about the painting in his

00:06:23.599 --> 00:06:27.270
study, and the "ding, ding, ding" he says
at the end of the film which references the

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.570
ping sound that motherboxes make in the comics.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.419
So guys, what do you think about the deleted
scenes?

00:06:32.419 --> 00:06:35.530
Do you think they would have made the movie
better or would they have made it more complicated?

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:39.060
As always, I'd love to hear what you've got
to say in the comments below.

